  "body": "The Sodick LN2W post (PR #4065, issue #4045) refuses control-side wire offset. The post writes only the wire-centre path. A machine owner (Sodick AQ600L, LN2W control) gave the rules for control-side offset on 2026-11-25.\n\nRules from the owner:\n- H numbers are consecutive integers from `H001`. A 3-pass cut uses `H001`, `H002`, `H003`. The operator sets their values at the control.\n- The lead-in must be at least the wire radius long (the same rule as a mill cutter radius).\n- `G41`/`G42` goes on the lead-in line, or on its own line immediately before the lead-in. The own-line form is easier.\n- `G40` must go on a lead-out move.\n\nThe owner's example:\n\n```\nG54 G90\nG29\nT91\nT84\nT94\nC001\nG42 H001\nG01 Y10.\nX0.\nG40 Y0\n```\n\nOpen questions for the owner (ask before code):\n- What does `G29` do on this control, and is it required?\n- Which condition number goes with which pass (`C001` here, `C000` in the earlier kit)?\n\nWork:\n1. The post accepts compensation \"in control\" and \"wear\" for the LN2W dialect. It writes `G41`/`G42 Hnnn` on its own line before the lead-in, with H = pass number (from `H001`), and `G40` on the lead-out move.\n2. The post refuses a lead-in shorter than the wire radius, with a message that names the operation.\n3. The wire-centre path stays the default. Mark 21 output stays byte-identical.\n4. Goldens for the square and the 2-axis parts with offset on, rough plus skims.\n\nDone means: an LN2W program with control-side offset posts in the owner's form, a too-short lead-in is refused, and the existing LN2W and Mark 21 goldens do not change.\n\nRefs #4045. Part of the Sodick work in #617 and #1500. Do not start before PR #4065 merges (this changes the same post).\n",
